        <item>
            <title>1.1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:34:38 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/lazzyms/toolbox</link>
            <sparkle:version>23</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Toolbox now lives in the menu bar.** The hammer icon opens a panel with the full
toolbox — pick a tool, drop files in, run it — so you never need a window. Switch on
**Hide Dock icon** in **Settings → General** and Toolbox leaves the Dock entirely: no
Dock icon, no app switcher entry, no window at login. It takes effect immediately, no
relaunch, and the menu bar icon stays available so there's always a way back.

**Open Toolbox at login** is in the same place, for either mode.

Everything else is unchanged: files are still processed entirely on your Mac.

[Full changes](https://github.com/lazzyms/toolbox/compare/v1.0.0...v1.1.0)
]]></description>
